        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. New round of Israel-Lebanon talks opens after Israeli strikes Middle East Issued on: 03/06/2026 - 11:53 Modified: 03/06/2026 - 11:53 The ambassadors of Israel and Lebanon began a new round of direct talks in Washington on after US President Donald Trump said he had received commitments to de-escalation from both sides. The fourth meeting between representatives of the two countries, which do not have diplomatic relations, is taking place at the State Department and is scheduled to last two days. It comes as Israeli drone strikes on southern Lebanon on June 2 killed eight people, including two children and their father, and as Iran-backed Hezbollah continued launching drones at Israeli troops. Kuwait airport hit by Iranian drones as US-Iran talks stall 03/06/2026 Middle East Trump's acknowledgment of Hezbollah 'utterly humiliating' for Netanyahu 02/06/2026 Middle East 'Healthy consensus in Israel' on pursuing Lebanon campaign, expert says 01/06/2026 Middle East 'Most extreme right-wing fringes of Netanyahu govt call for far greater military action in Lebanon' 01/06/2026 Middle East Kuwait intercepts drones, missiles as US and Iran trade fire 01/06/2026 Middle East Is Israel seeking free reign from US in Lebanon? 01/06/2026 Middle East What is Lebanon's Beaufort Castle, and why have Israeli forces captured it? 31/05/2026 Middle East Israel seizes strategic Beaufort Castle in Lebanon, issues new evacuation orders 31/05/2026 Middle East Three months after the strike, Iranian families still mourn Minab's children 31/05/2026 Middle East"
